note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note bridge/shlib/ampqmd.om: CUDApp's src/omega_ampere_qmd.c (84b524ca, default build) in Omega: the two C entry
note points omega_ampere_policy and omega_ampere_build_qmd over the Ampere QMD unit. Composed after
note gpu/nvidia/om/encoder/amp_runtime.om and amp_qmd.om into one object and built by bridge/shlib/shlib.om from
note ampqmd.tsv: both are frame exports under the lock row's pthread mutex, because the C pointers are copied
note through the states (memcpy) and the states are one per process.
note States (ampqmd.tsv, frame words 8..10): AqM the 16-word request, AqQ the 256 QMD bytes, AqLock the mutex;
note frame word 11 is the address of the caller's stack arguments (omega_ampere_build_qmd's registers and
note shared_bytes, AAPCS64 arguments 9 and 10).
note Results as the C: 0 when amp_qmd accepts, -1 when it refuses or a pointer the C checks is NULL; the QMD is
note written to q only on acceptance. A trap answers -1 (the TRAP value), as the C does when its bridge call
note fails.
extern fn memcpy d ulong s ulong n ulong to ulong
note amp_qmd op over the request in m; on acceptance the 256 bytes are copied to the C pointer q when it is not
note NULL; 0 or -1
fn aq_run fr view ulong 12 op ulong m edit ulong 16 q edit uchar 256 to int
if ne amp_qmd op m q 1
ret -1
end
d = get fr 1
if eq op 1
d = get fr 0
end
if ne d 0
z = memcpy d get fr 9 256
end
ret 0
end
note int omega_ampere_policy(const uint64_t m[16], uint32_t q[64]): x0 m, x1 q (NULL: the C's scratch)
export fn omega_ampere_policy fr view ulong 12 m edit ulong 16 q edit uchar 256 to int
if eq get fr 0 0
ret -1
end
z = memcpy get fr 8 get fr 0 128
ret aq_run fr 0 m q
end
note int omega_ampere_build_qmd(uint32_t q[64], uint64_t code, uint64_t cbank, uint64_t semaphore, uint32_t tx,
note uint32_t ty, uint32_t gx, uint32_t gy, uint32_t registers, uint32_t shared_bytes): x0 q, x1..x3 the 64-bit
note words, x4..x7 tx ty gx gy (their low 32 bits), the caller's stack words 0 and 1 registers and shared_bytes
note (their low 32 bits); a[9..15] zero, as the C's initializer
export fn omega_ampere_build_qmd fr view ulong 12 m edit ulong 16 q edit uchar 256 to int
if eq get fr 0 0
ret -1
end
for i ulong 16
put m i 0
end
z = memcpy add get fr 8 56 get fr 11 16
put m 7 and get m 7 4294967295
put m 8 and get m 8 4294967295
for i ulong 3
put m i get fr add i 1
end
for i ulong 4
put m add i 3 and get fr add i 4 4294967295
end
ret aq_run fr 1 m q
end
